{%- comment -%}Speed. 1) Instant pages: when a link is about to be opened (finger down, or the pointer resting on it) the browser starts loading that page ahead, so it opens almost at once; cart, checkout, account and search are never loaded ahead. 2) Eco mode: on a slow phone, in battery or data saver, or when the page cannot keep a smooth frame rate, html gets the class bls-lite: the space background stands still and the bars stop blurring what is behind them. The choice is kept for the visit, so later pages start in the right mode.{%- endcomment -%}
